  "question": {
    "text": "A point on the ellipse, $4 x^2+9 y^2=36$, where the normal is parallel to the line, $4 x-2 y-5=0$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rZCUQ",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{9}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z1l4H",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{8}{5},-\\frac{9}{5}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ws0yd",
      "text": "\n$\\left(-\\frac{9}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "clc6I",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{8}{5}, \\frac{9}{5}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given ellipse is $4 x^2+9 y^2=36$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{x^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{4}=1\n$$\nNormal at the point is parallel to the line\n$$\n4 x-2 y-5=0\n$$\nSlope of normal $=2$\nSlope of tangent $=\\frac{-1}{2}$\nPoint of contact to ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$\nand line is $\\left(\\frac{a^2 m}{\\sqrt{a^2 m^2+b^2}}, \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a^2 m^2+b^2}}\\right)$\nNow, $a^2=9, b^2=4$\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad \\text { Point }=\\left(\\frac{-9}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}\\right)\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
